 "intro_html": "Japanese fried chicken. Poking the thighs lets the soy–sake–mirin marinade in; tapioca starch (not flour) with little fork-made crumbs gives the craggy crunch; and <b>frying twice</b> — pale first, rest, then dark — makes it crisp without drying it out.",
