 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cut the deboned thighs into 4–5 cm pieces.</li><li><b>Poke them all over</b> with a sharp fork or skewer — both sides — so the marinade gets in.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Cut and poke",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Poke every piece all over with a sharp fork — both sides — so the marinade gets in.",
      "src": "illustrations/karaage/1-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/karaage/1.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~8 min",
   "title": "Cut and poke",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "500 g",
     "name_html": "Boneless chicken thighs, skin on"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Mix the marinade:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>ginger, grated <span class=\"amt\">10 g (2 tsp)</span></li><li>garlic, grated <span class=\"amt\">2 cloves</span></li><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\">1 tbsp</span></li><li>soy sauce <span class=\"amt\">2 tbsp</span></li><li>sake <span class=\"amt\">1 tbsp</span></li><li>ground pepper <span class=\"amt\">¼ tsp</span></li><li>oyster sauce <span class=\"amt\">1 tsp</span></li><li>brown sugar <span class=\"amt\">1 tsp</span></li></ul></li><li>Toss the chicken in it and marinate in the fridge.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Marinate",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Mix the marinade, then toss the chicken in it.",
      "src": "illustrations/karaage/2-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/karaage/2.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "30 min – overnight",
   "title": "Marinate",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Pour off and discard the excess marinade.</li><li>Mix <b>1 tbsp flour and 1 tbsp tapioca starch</b> into the chicken until every piece has a tacky coat.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Pour off, then flour + starch",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Tilt the bowl and pour off the excess marinade, holding the chicken back.",
      "src": "illustrations/karaage/3-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Mix in 1 tbsp flour and 1 tbsp tapioca starch until every piece is tacky.",
      "src": "illustrations/karaage/3-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/karaage/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3 min",
   "title": "Pour off, then flour + starch",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "1 tbsp",
     "name_html": "Flour (into the chicken)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "1 tbsp",
     "name_html": "Tapioca starch (into the chicken)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Spread the tapioca starch over a cutting board.</li><li>Make the little round bits: drizzle a teaspoon or two of water (or leftover marinade) over part of it and work it with a fork into small crumbs and pebbles.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Starch board and crumbs",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Drizzle a little water over part of the starch and work it with a fork into small crumbs.",
      "src": "illustrations/karaage/4-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/karaage/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min",
   "title": "Starch board and crumbs",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "~80 g",
     "name_html": "Tapioca starch (on the board)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "1–2 tsp",
     "name_html": "Water or leftover marinade (for crumbs)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Heat 3–4 cm of oil in a heavy pot to <b>180 °C</b>.</p>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-high",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Heat the oil",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/karaage/5.webp",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~10 min",
   "title": "Heat the oil",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "enough for 3–4 cm depth",
     "name_html": "Neutral oil"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>While the oil heats, roll each piece in the starch and crumbs on the board, pressing so the bits stick.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Roll in starch",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Roll each piece in the starch and press it onto the crumbs so they stick.",
      "src": "illustrations/karaage/6-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/karaage/6.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~4 min",
   "title": "Roll in starch",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lower in a batch without crowding.</li><li>Fry a couple of minutes until <b>light yellow / light orange</b>.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "180 °C oil",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "First fry — pale",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Lower the pieces in one at a time, away from you — don't crowd the pot.",
      "src": "illustrations/karaage/7-how1.webp"
     }
